---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Lumen"
  description="Lumen is an open source, offline-first, privacy-by-design assistant for people with a limitation."
  lang="en"
  altHref="/"
>
  <h1>Lumen</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    An open source, offline-first, privacy-by-design assistant that turns a smartphone into help
    for people with a limitation: seeing, hearing, speaking, reading and studying, remembering,
    moving, and staying safe.
  </p>

  <p>
    Lumen is built for the <strong>GF Marilli Prize</strong> by HackersGen. A single shared
    multimodal engine, the "senses engine" (vision, audio, text), powers eight modules delivered as
    independent plugins.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>
    On first launch, a short "who are you" onboarding (five questions, by voice or by images) turns
    on only the modules a person needs. The interface adapts accordingly: voice and large buttons
    for low vision, a fully visual interface with vibration for deaf users, a simplified layout for
    elderly users, a complete layout for students.
  </p>

  <div class="notice">
    Every essential feature works with no network connection. No audio or image ever leaves the
    device unless the person explicitly chooses to share it.
  </div>

  <h2>Project status</h2>
  <p>
    Lumen is in active, open source development. The senses engine (<a
      href="https://github.com/lumen-assistive/lumen-core">lumen-core</a
    >) and the plugin SDK (<a href="https://github.com/lumen-assistive/lumen-sdk">lumen-sdk</a>) are
    the first published components. See the <a href="/en/modules/">Modules</a> page for the status
    of each module.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not publish user data, metrics, or partnerships until they are real and verifiable.
    Results from real user testing and any collaborations will be published here once available.
  </p>
</Layout>
